 "section_summary": "This section comprises U.S. State Department records from August to September 1934 concerning Japanese internal affairs, foreign relations, and economic conditions. It contains docket sheets indexing monthly political reports from Japan (1934-1938), briefing memoranda prepared by the Division of Far Eastern Affairs, and Embassy Tokyo Despatch No. 917 transmitting Report No. 94 for July 1934, alongside the covering despatch for August 1934. Key subjects include the collapse of the Saito Cabinet and installation of the Okada Cabinet, Japan's naval disarmament stance, border and diplomatic issues regarding Manchukuo and the Soviet Union, and foreign trade negotiations.",
