   "start_page": 5,
   "summary": "This memorandum highlights significant items in the Tokyo Embassy's July 1934 report for State Department officials. It discusses constitutional amendments in Brazil restricting Japanese immigration and foreign-owned newspapers, as well as Peruvian legislation mandating that 80 percent of commercial employees be Peruvian citizens. It also outlines Japanese Foreign Office plans to strengthen the international standing of Manchukuo, customs house proposals in Chosen, and negotiations at the Soviet-Manchukuo Waterways Conference.",
