   "start_page": 8,
   "summary": "Ambassador Joseph C. Grew transmits Report No. 94 reviewing political, economic, and diplomatic conditions in Japan during July 1934. The report details the resignation of Premier Saito following government corruption scandals and the formation of a new cabinet under Admiral Keisuke Okada, discussing political party reactions, army defense platforms, and reactionary plots. In foreign relations, it reviews American-Japanese relations, Ambassador Saito's consultations, naval disarmament demands, Shanhaikwan border issues with Great Britain, Indo-Japanese and Dutch-Japanese trade parleys, and Soviet-Japanese railway and fisheries disputes. It further examines Japanese financial and industrial conditions, agrarian distress, labor strikes, and lists all despatches and telegrams sent to the Department during July.",
