   "summary": "This internal memorandum summarizes key points from Tokyo's monthly report for August 1934. It highlights Japanese assurances that American firms in Dairen will not be forced to contribute to municipal air defense funds, and notes British assurances that garrison maneuvers will not take place on Manchukuo's borders. It also notes French pressure to balance trade, Chinese establishment of border customs stations, projected air lines, arrests of suspected communists in Hiroshima, and Japanese plans to open legations in Africa and Latin America.",
